---

<Base title="OpenTUI - A Reference Manual for Native Terminal Interfaces">
  <div class="editorial-wrapper">
    <div class="editorial-container">

      <!-- Editorial Masthead -->
      <div class="editorial-masthead">
        <div class="editorial-masthead-title">OPENTUI REFERENCE MANUAL</div>
        <div class="editorial-masthead-nav">
          <a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a>
          <a href="#lab">Laboratory</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Documentation</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Editorial Hero Header -->
      <header class="editorial-hero">
        <h1 class="editorial-title">OpenTUI</h1>
        <p class="editorial-subtitle">
          A reference manual for people who design and build native terminal user interfaces.
        </p>
        <div class="editorial-byline">
          <div>Written and engineered by the <span>OpenTUI Contributors</span>.</div>
          <div>&copy; 2026 Anomaly &middot; Version 0.5.1 &middot; 58 Chapters</div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Editorial Multi-Column Flow with Masterpiece Vector Figures -->
      <div class="editorial-flow">
        
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          Have you ever wondered how a terminal screen knows how to render rich, interactive user interfaces at sixty frames per second without flickering? In classical computing, the terminal is not a bitmap canvas with hardware scanouts; it is a stream of character cells transmitted over standard input and output pipes. When a modern application updates its state, re-emitting the entire terminal grid saturates the pseudo-terminal buffer, causing severe screen tearing and latency.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_001: The Anatomy of a Character Cell -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_001</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ 16-BYTE CELL STRIDE ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 220" width="380" height="220" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Isometric Box Layer 1: UTF-32 Codepoint -->
              <g transform="translate(40, 20)">
                <path d="M150 10 L270 75 L150 140 L30 75 Z" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.08)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <path d="M30 75 L30 95 L150 160 L150 140 Z" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.15)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <path d="M270 75 L270 95 L150 160 L150 140 Z" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <text x="150" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="currentColor">0x0000: char_codepoint (u32)</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Isometric Layer 2: 24-Bit FG & BG RGBA -->
              <g transform="translate(40, 50)">
                <path d="M150 10 L270 75 L150 140 L30 75 Z" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.08)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <path d="M30 75 L30 90 L150 155 L150 140 Z" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <path d="M270 75 L270 90 L150 155 L150 140 Z" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <text x="150" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="currentColor">0x0004: fg_rgba &amp; bg_rgba (24-bit TrueColor)</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Isometric Layer 3: Style Flags & Damage Mask -->
              <g transform="translate(40, 78)">
                <path d="M150 10 L270 75 L150 140 L30 75 Z" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.08)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <path d="M30 75 L30 88 L150 153 L150 140 Z" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.15)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <path d="M270 75 L270 88 L150 153 L150 140 Z" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <text x="150" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="currentColor">0x000C: style_flags &amp; damage_mask (u16)</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Exploded memory layout of an OpenTUI terminal cell. Each cell is packed into a compact 16-byte contiguous stride, aligning perfectly with CPU cache lines for high-throughput raster passes.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">&copy; 2026 OPENTUI</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">STRIDE: 16B</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Because the terminal is arranged as a discrete matrix of rows and columns, a character is not merely a scalar glyph. It is an atomic structure containing a UTF-32 code point, a 24-bit TrueColor foreground vector, a 24-bit background vector, 16-bit typography attributes (bold, italics, underline, inverse), and a damage tracking bitmask. On an 80&times;24 terminal, this complete double-buffered matrix occupies exactly <strong>30.7 kilobytes</strong>.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_002: The Differential Damage Loop -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_002</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ DIFFERENTIAL DAMAGE LOOP ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 180" width="380" height="180" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Buffer A -->
              <rect x="20" y="30" width="120" height="90" fill="var(--background)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="80" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">PREVIOUS BUFFER</text>
              <line x1="20" y1="60" x2="140" y2="60" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>
              <line x1="20" y1="90" x2="140" y2="90" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

              <!-- Diff Comparator -->
              <path d="M160 75 L200 75" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
              <text x="180" y="65" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--emerald-600)">DIFF</text>

              <!-- Buffer B with Damage Box -->
              <rect x="220" y="30" width="120" height="90" fill="var(--background)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="280" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">CURRENT BUFFER</text>
              <rect x="245" y="45" width="55" height="35" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15)" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="272" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--emerald-600)">DIRTY [X, Y, W, H]</text>

              <!-- Escape Stream Output -->
              <rect x="20" y="140" width="320" height="28" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.03)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8"/>
              <text x="30" y="158" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">{"\\x1b[4;12H\\x1b[38;2;16;185;129mACTIVE\\x1b[0m"}</text>
              <text x="330" y="158" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--emerald-600)">-99.1% BYTES</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Double-buffered cell diffing isolates modified subregions. Rather than retransmitting 3,840 bytes for a full screen repaint, OpenTUI emits concise ANSI cursor hops, slashing bandwidth and eliminating flicker.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">&copy; 2026 OPENTUI</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">VT100 DELTA</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          To achieve liquid 60 FPS motion without screen tearing, OpenTUI employs a <strong>differential damage tracking pipeline</strong>. On every frame tick, the engine compares previous and current character cells, isolates the minimal damaged bounding box [x₁, y₁, x₂, y₂], and encodes delta run-length ANSI sequences. A state change that modifies only a status label emits less than 40 bytes instead of 3,840 bytes—an I/O bandwidth savings exceeding <strong>99.1%</strong>.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_003: Continuous Flexbox to Discrete Grid Quantization -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_003</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ YOGA GRID QUANTIZATION ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 170" width="380" height="170" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Continuous Float Box -->
              <rect x="30" y="30" width="140" height="70" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.08)" stroke="var(--cobalt-600)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
              <text x="100" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--cobalt-600)">FLOAT: w=33.333% (15.998)</text>

              <!-- Quantization Arrow -->
              <path d="M185 65 L215 65" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
              <text x="200" y="55" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="currentColor">FLOOR(X)</text>

              <!-- Discrete Integer Cells -->
              <g transform="translate(225, 30)">
                <rect x="0" y="0" width="130" height="70" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.15)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <line x1="26" y1="0" x2="26" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <line x1="52" y1="0" x2="52" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <line x1="78" y1="0" x2="78" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <line x1="104" y1="0" x2="104" y2="70" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                <text x="65" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">16 COLUMNS</text>
              </g>
              
              <!-- Rulers -->
              <text x="190" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--text-muted)">UNICODE 16.0 WCWIDTH: 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 (2 CH) &middot; CJK (2 CH)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Compiling continuous Yoga CSS flexbox geometry into rigid integer terminal cells without edge collisions or text clipping.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">&copy; 2026 OPENTUI</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">CSS &rarr; GRID</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Or perhaps you have wondered how web-style CSS layout can exist inside a terminal without a bloated browser runtime? Web flexbox operates in continuous subpixel coordinates (33.333% width, 1.5rem padding). But a terminal screen is an immutable integer matrix. OpenTUI embeds the native <strong>Yoga C engine</strong> and executes an exact quantization pass: fractional bounds snap to integer boundaries, border strokes share single-cell seams, and text wrapping dynamically evaluates Unicode 16.0 grapheme widths (<code>wcwidth</code>) including zero-width joiners.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_004: 4x4 RGBA SIMD Vector Lane Transformation -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_004</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ 4×4 SIMD VECTOR LANES ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 160" width="380" height="160" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Matrix Equation -->
              <g transform="translate(30, 25)">
                <!-- Left Vector -->
                <text x="15" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">R'</text>
                <text x="15" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">G'</text>
                <text x="15" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">B'</text>
                <text x="15" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">A'</text>
                <path d="M5 10 L0 10 L0 95 L5 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path d="M25 10 L30 10 L30 95 L25 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                
                <text x="45" y="55" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">=</text>

                <!-- 4x4 Matrix -->
                <g transform="translate(65, 0)">
                  <path d="M5 10 L0 10 L0 95 L5 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                  <path d="M145 10 L150 10 L150 95 L145 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                  <text x="20" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.39</text>
                  <text x="55" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.76</text>
                  <text x="90" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.18</text>
                  <text x="125" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  
                  <text x="20" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.34</text>
                  <text x="55" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.68</text>
                  <text x="90" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.16</text>
                  <text x="125" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>

                  <text x="20" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.27</text>
                  <text x="55" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.53</text>
                  <text x="90" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.13</text>
                  <text x="125" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>

                  <text x="20" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  <text x="55" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  <text x="90" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0.00</text>
                  <text x="125" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">1.00</text>
                </g>

                <!-- Input Vector -->
                <g transform="translate(230, 0)">
                  <text x="15" y="25" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">R</text>
                  <text x="15" y="45" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">G</text>
                  <text x="15" y="65" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">B</text>
                  <text x="15" y="85" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">A</text>
                  <path d="M5 10 L0 10 L0 95 L5 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                  <path d="M25 10 L30 10 L30 95 L25 95" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                </g>
              </g>
              <text x="190" y="145" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--amber-600)">AVX2 / ARM NEON 4-WIDE VECTOR REGISTER</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Linear algebra vector transformations executed across 4-wide SIMD lanes. Instant amber CRT phosphor emulation, sepia grading, and contrast masks without traversing the DOM tree.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">&copy; 2026 OPENTUI</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">SIMD 4×4</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Before character cells are serialized into ANSI truecolor sequences, OpenTUI applies vectorized linear algebra across foreground and background color vectors using SIMD lanes: [R', G', B', A']ᵀ = M₄ₓ₄ &middot; [R, G, B, A]ᵀ. This allows real-time color grading, scanline attenuation, sepia archiving, and CRT phosphor emulation at zero per-cell runtime cost.
        </p>

        <!-- FIG_005: Terminal Graphics Protocol Resolution -->
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <span class="fig-tag-top-left">FIG_005</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-top-right">[ GRAPHICS PROTOCOL RESOLUTION ]</span>
          
          <div class="figure-canvas-wrap">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 150" width="380" height="150" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <!-- Tier 1 -->
              <rect x="20" y="20" width="75" height="85" fill="rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.1)" stroke="var(--cobalt-600)" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="57" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 1</text>
              <text x="57" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--cobalt-600)">KITTY</text>
              <text x="57" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">APC PNG/RGB</text>

              <!-- Tier 2 -->
              <rect x="105" y="20" width="75" height="85" fill="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.1)" stroke="var(--amber-600)" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="142" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 2</text>
              <text x="142" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--amber-600)">SIXEL</text>
              <text x="142" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">6-PX BANDS</text>

              <!-- Tier 3 -->
              <rect x="190" y="20" width="85" height="85" fill="rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1)" stroke="var(--emerald-600)" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="232" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 3</text>
              <text x="232" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--emerald-600)">QUADRANT</text>
              <text x="232" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">▀ ▄ █ HALF-BLOCK</text>

              <!-- Tier 4 -->
              <rect x="285" y="20" width="75" height="85" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.03)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              <text x="322" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">TIER 4</text>
              <text x="322" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="currentColor">ASCII</text>
              <text x="322" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="8" fill="var(--text-muted)">░ ▒ ▓ HALFTONE</text>
              
              <text x="190" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--text-muted)">RUNTIME DEC / OSC CAPABILITY PROBING</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="figure-caption-text">
            Automatic protocol negotiation. OpenTUI queries the host emulator at startup and seamlessly routes graphics across hardware Kitty protocols, DEC Sixel scanlines, or Unicode quadrant half-blocks.
          </div>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-left">&copy; 2026 OPENTUI</span>
          <span class="fig-tag-bottom-right">AUTODETECT</span>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Terminal graphic capabilities vary widely across platforms. OpenTUI probes terminal device attributes at startup and dynamically routes between Kitty graphics (PNG/RGB chunking over APC escapes), Sixel 6-pixel raster bands, and Unicode 2&times;2 quadrant half-block characters (<code>▀▄█</code>) with 24-bit TrueColor foreground and background.
        </p>

        <p>
          All of this machinery is unified through a <strong>zero-allocation C ABI</strong> written in native Zig. Whether you construct terminal applications with declarative React 19 JSX, Solid.js fine-grained signals, or bare-metal Zig, the rendering engine operates with zero garbage collection pauses and uncompromising deterministic performance.
        </p>

      </div>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           TABLE OF CONTENTS: V1.0 ARCHIVAL INDEX
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="toc-section" id="toc">
        <div class="toc-header">
          <h2 class="toc-heading">Table of Contents.</h2>
          <span class="toc-version">VOLUME I &middot; SPECIFICATION 2026</span>
        </div>

        <div class="toc-grid">
          {tocData.map((part) => (
            <div class="toc-part-card">
              <div class="toc-part-label">{part.part}</div>
              <ul class="toc-chapter-list">
                {part.chapters.map((chap) => (
                  <li class="toc-chapter-item">
                    <a href={chap.slug}>
                      <span>{chap.title}</span>
                      <span class="chapter-words">{chap.words}</span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================================
           INTERACTIVE LABORATORY DRAFTING BENCH
           ========================================================================= -->
      <section class="bench-section" id="lab">
        <div class="bench-header">
          <h2 class="bench-heading">Interactive Laboratory.</h2>
          <div class="bench-sub">CALIBRATE THE NATIVE RENDERING PIPELINE IN REAL TIME</div>
        </div>

        <div class="bench-viewport">
          <div class="bench-tabs-bar">
            <div class="bench-tabs-list" role="tablist">
              <button role="tab" class="bench-tab" data-bench-tab="diff" aria-selected="true">FIG_001: Delta Stream</button>
              <button role="tab" class="bench-tab" data-bench-tab="matrix" aria-selected="false">FIG_003: Color Matrix</button>
